# Build context = repo root. The image needs client/ (source), docs/changelog/
# (the title screen's changelog viewer imports it with ?raw), and the SERVER —
# main.go, cmd/, internal/, go.mod, go.sum — since the image is now one binary
# that serves the client rather than nginx serving files.
**/node_modules
client/dist
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# The server's own stores, if a local run created them. They are data, and a
# 20 GB artifact directory in a build context is a slow surprise.
worlds
artifacts
saves

# Generated: the image builds its own from source in the web stage, and a stale
# copy from the host would be the exact drift the single-image design avoids.
baker.mjs
casas-eternas

docs
*.md
# …except the docs tree, which the web stage renders into the documentation
# site (npm run build:docs) — the negations must come after the patterns they
# undo. ideas/ is deliberately NOT re-included: private material never enters
# the build context at all, on top of the generator never reading it and the
# runtime image only receiving the rendered docs-dist.
!docs/**
docs/ideas
docs/ideas/**

notes-dont-process.md
GPU_TECTONICS_PLAN.md
